.TH GEN 1.SH NAMEgen \- the frame of a new C source file.SH SYNOPSIS\fBgen\fR\-p|\-m|\-t|\-f name.SH DESCRIPTION\fBgen\fRwrites the skeleton of a new C file to\fIname\fB.c\fR-- a header block for the file name and type, a description, theauthors, and a version history with today's date, followed by thesectioned comments of the kind being started.  Exactly one kind must bechosen:.TP 12\fB\-p\fRa program..TP 12\fB\-m\fRa module..TP 12\fB\-t\fRa type declaration..TP 12\fB\-f\fRa function declaration..PPThe authors' line is filled with its own author's name and address,M. Moser of Kaufbeuren; edit it..SH SEE ALSOif, run